    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0661" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.711/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-26T13:00:00+08:00">March 26, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 26—9:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to this Consulate General’s telegram of February 20, 2 p.m.<anchor
                        n="77" xml:id="d629-f1"/> The postal ban on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shanghai Evening Post</hi> was removed on March 23. (Repeated to the
                    Legation.)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
